WEBVTT

NOTE
Canonical written narration timed from the exact local narration render receipt.
Pronunciation-only substitutions are intentionally absent from caption text.

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.579
This chapter asks a specific question: AI computation increasingly crosses distrust

2
00:00:04.579 --> 00:00:07.866
boundaries: a user may need to hide inputs,

3
00:00:07.866 --> 00:00:12.386
a provider may need to protect weights, an auditor may need

4
00:00:12.386 --> 00:00:14.440
to verify the executed artifact,

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:20.482
and every party may need output integrity without granting another party

6
00:00:20.482 --> 00:00:25.148
unrestricted custody. Ordinary transport encryption ends before computation begins.

7
00:00:25.148 --> 00:00:30.850
The tempting shortcut is insufficient: Privacy policy governs permitted information use,

8
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.960
while hardware custody governs stored artifacts.

9
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:41.750
Neither supplies a guarantee-by-guarantee execution contract covering input confidentiality, model confidentiality,

10
00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:48.523
computation integrity, output authenticity, attestation freshness, leakage, verifier policy, cost,

11
00:00:48.523 --> 00:00:50.555
and failure recovery.

12
00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:56.829
The chapter's core claim is this: Confidential and verifiable AI requires

13
00:00:56.829 --> 00:01:01.988
a compositional execution contract that names the adversary, protected assets,

14
00:01:01.988 --> 00:01:07.662
permitted leakage, trust anchors, proof or attestation statement, verifier policy, freshness,

15
00:01:07.662 --> 00:01:09.210
revocation, performance budget,

16
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:14.902
and authorization boundary; no primitive or attestation may be treated as

17
00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:19.280
proof of semantic correctness, legitimate purpose, or end-to-end privacy.

18
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:26.498
Express the requested guarantee vector separately for input privacy, model privacy,

19
00:01:26.498 --> 00:01:32.125
intermediate-state privacy, computation integrity, output authenticity, availability, and auditability.

20
00:01:32.465 --> 00:01:38.138
Choose among FHE, MPC, zero-knowledge proofs, confidential execution, private retrieval,

21
00:01:38.138 --> 00:01:44.378
differential privacy, or hybrid composition against an explicit adversary and leakage

22
00:01:44.378 --> 00:01:44.945
model.

23
00:01:45.545 --> 00:01:49.575
A concrete implementation trace makes the proposal testable.

24
00:01:49.915 --> 00:01:56.014
A guarantee matrix and local demonstration for one bounded inference operation

25
00:01:56.014 --> 00:02:02.114
with explicit adversary and leakage models, artifact and configuration commitments, freshness,

26
00:02:02.114 --> 00:02:05.995
independent verification, native-versus-protected latency and cost accounting,

27
00:02:06.335 --> 00:02:12.153
negative tests for replay and mismatched artifacts, and a no-authorization non-claim.

28
00:02:12.153 --> 00:02:17.443
Choose among FHE, MPC, zero-knowledge proofs, confidential execution, private retrieval,

29
00:02:17.443 --> 00:02:23.261
differential privacy, or hybrid composition against an explicit adversary and leakage

30
00:02:23.261 --> 00:02:23.790
model.

31
00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:29.554
Bind code, model, configuration, data commitments, platform state, nonce or epoch,

32
00:02:29.554 --> 00:02:34.485
and policy identity into evidence that a distinct verifier appraises.

33
00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:40.756
Keep cryptographic correctness, attested identity, model quality, semantic validity, user authorization,

34
00:02:40.756 --> 00:02:44.530
and lawful purpose as separate claim classes.

35
00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:51.104
The design can still fail. Guarantee laundering collapses confidentiality, integrity, privacy,

36
00:02:51.104 --> 00:02:57.079
authorization, and correctness into one secure-compute label. Stale or replayed attestation

37
00:02:57.079 --> 00:03:02.510
is accepted after artifact, platform, policy, or revocation state changed.

38
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:08.731
Side channels, outputs, access patterns, logs, caches, or failure timing leak

39
00:03:08.731 --> 00:03:14.078
protected information. The proved computation faithfully executes the wrong model,

40
00:03:14.078 --> 00:03:18.355
wrong preprocessing, wrong policy, or semantically invalid relation.

41
00:03:18.695 --> 00:03:22.664
The correct response is to stop, narrow, quarantine, compensate,

42
00:03:22.664 --> 00:03:27.075
or retain an owned residual rather than narrate uncertainty away.

43
00:03:27.675 --> 00:03:32.721
This chapter remains Design rationale at argument support. Its contracts, examples,

44
00:03:32.721 --> 00:03:36.850
tests, or local artifacts establish only their encoded scope.

45
00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:41.896
The chapter names proof targets rather than pretending they are already

46
00:03:41.896 --> 00:03:42.355
closed.

47
00:03:42.695 --> 00:03:48.782
A finite protected-execution record may hand off only when guarantees, adversary,

48
00:03:48.782 --> 00:03:54.870
leakage, artifact, freshness, verifier policy, fallback, and unsupported properties are explicit;

49
00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:59.850
no theorem proves semantic correctness, authorization, or end-to-end privacy.

50
00:04:00.190 --> 00:04:04.879
An attestation proves only the appraised statement about a measured environment;

51
00:04:04.879 --> 00:04:08.290
it does not prove trustworthy intent, correct policy,

52
00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:09.995
or correct output meaning.

53
00:04:10.595 --> 00:04:15.559
No chapter claim or evidence state is promoted by this visual.

54
00:04:15.559 --> 00:04:20.523
A named mechanism is not proof of correct implementation or useful

55
00:04:20.523 --> 00:04:25.487
deployment. A local check or formal model does not establish real-world

56
00:04:25.487 --> 00:04:30.000
enforcement. No safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI, or ASI conclusion follows.

57
00:04:30.340 --> 00:04:34.815
These boundaries matter because an explanatory derivative is useful only if

58
00:04:34.815 --> 00:04:38.070
it preserves the evidence ceiling of its source.

59
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:43.716
At most, this visual explains the chapter's design rationale at argument

60
00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:48.303
support; it adds no empirical, deployment, safety, transfer, state-of-the-art, AGI,

61
00:04:48.303 --> 00:04:53.349
or ASI result. The next chapter is Model-Weight Custody and Hardware

62
00:04:53.349 --> 00:04:54.725
Roots of Trust.

63
00:04:55.065 --> 00:05:00.906
It takes responsibility for A system can govern runtime tool authority

64
00:05:00.906 --> 00:05:06.748
while model weights, optimizer state, adapters, quantizations, checkpoints, caches, recovery images,

65
00:05:06.748 --> 00:05:12.589
extracted equivalents, and recipient derivatives are copied, reconstructed, decrypted, loaded, served,

66
00:05:12.589 --> 00:05:13.120
revoked.
